Kube-proxy:
kube-proxy is a Kubernetes networking component that runs on every node. It watches Services and EndpointSlices from the API Server and programs network rules using iptables or IPVS. When traffic is sent to a Service ClusterIP, the Linux kernel uses those rules to load balance the request to one of the backend Pods. In modern eBPF-based solutions like Cilium, kube-proxy can be completely replaced and Service load balancing is done directly by eBPF programs inside the kernel.

