Senior-Level Interview Answer

CNI is the networking framework used by Kubernetes to provide IP addresses and connectivity to Pods. When a Pod is created, Kubelet invokes the CNI plugin, which configures the network namespace, assigns an IP, and sets up routes. Common CNIs include AWS VPC CNI, Cilium, Calico, and Flannel. Modern environments increasingly adopt Cilium because it uses eBPF for routing, load balancing, security, and observability with lower overhead than iptables-based solutions.

